  "sections": [
    {
      "sectionId": "section-introduction",
      "heading": "Introduction",
      "sourceAnchor": "introduction",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "DnD 5.5’s "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Fey Sentinel feat",
              "href": "https://www.dndbeyond.com/feats/2097423-fey-sentinel"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", introduced in “D&D Beyond Drops”, leans into Fey mischief with the ability to teleport, to turn invisible, and to cast some Druid spells."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The Rogue may be the best character to use Fey Sentinel. You can use Fey Pact to get True Strike using your mental ability score of choice, then use it for all of your attacks. Fey Sentinel lets you increase that ability score, making it easy to justify at level 4. Fey Shift will then let you teleport literally every round. You can use Cunning Action (Dash) and teleport half your speed as a Bonus Action with no usage limitation."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-introduction-3",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Fey Sentinel requires the "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Fey Pact",
              "href": "https://rpgbot.net/2024-dnd/feats/fey-pact/"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " feat."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-ability-score-increase",
      "heading": "Ability Score Increase",
      "sourceAnchor": "ability-score-increase",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-ability-score-increase-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Any mental ability score. This really emphasises that the feat is primarily intended for spellcasters."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-fading-target",
      "heading": "Fading Target",
      "sourceAnchor": "fading-target",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-fading-target-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Even better than casting shield, turning invisible makes you untargetable by many effects, especially spells. Unfortunately, it only lasts until the beginning of your turn, and it’s only once per day. You’re most likely to use this when you’re targeted by something with Multiattack."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-fey-shift",
      "heading": "Fey Shift",
      "sourceAnchor": "fey-shift",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-fey-shift-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Bottomless short-range teleportation. In combat, this is limited by how rarely most characters can justify taking the Dash action. Of course, the Monk and the Rogue are notable exceptions, and will enjoy their new-found ablity to absolutely ignore Opportunity Attacks and grapples."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-fey-shift-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Outside of combat, this is insanely powerful. Teleport over hazards. Teleport through windows and keyholdes. Send a familiar to sneak into places, then teleport through solid walls by percieving through their senses. Half your speed certainly isn’t a long distance, but that barely matters. 15 feet more most characters is still incredible."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-natures-roots",
      "heading": "Nature’s Roots",
      "sourceAnchor": "natures-roots",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-natures-roots-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Two are control spells that mostly work by imposing difficult terrain. They’re remain decently useful for yo’re pretty good, but a full spellcaster may find them obsolete beyond low levels."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-natures-roots-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "This is notably the first published feat in 5e/5.5 that gives you a level 3 spell (not counting Potent Dragonmark)."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-6",
      "heading": "What are DnD Beyond Drops?",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-6-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Starting in April of 2026, DnD Beyond Drops aim to release monthly content for DnD 5.5 accessible exclusively to users with a paid subscription to DnD Beyond. The included character options are shareable with subscriptions that allow content sharing. For more information, see the official "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "D&D Beyond Drops FAQ",
              "href": "https://dndbeyond-support.wizards.com/hc/en-us/sections/48937182240404"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ". The developers also posted "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "Reddit AMA discussing Drops",
              "href": "https://www.reddit.com/r/dndbeyond/comments/1t6f0pe/ama_with_ddb_executive_producer_drops_product/"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " when they were announced."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-6-2",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "We saw the first round of errata for Drops in "
            },
            {
              "type": "link",
              "text": "August of 2026",
              "href": "https://www.dndbeyond.com/posts/2222-d-d-beyonds-august-drop-sewers-and-treasures?icid_medium=organic&icid_source=homepage_drops&icid_campaign=2026_drops&icid_content=2026_hype"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", so it appears that WotC plans to continue supporting Drops and to update the published content."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
